      "id": 1,
      "text": "Welch was incorporated in 1894 and named after Isaiah A. Welch, a Confederate surveyor who plotted the town at Tug Fork and Elkhorn Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        5,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welch%2C_West_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Welch’s downtown is on the National Register of Historic Places, earning the town national recognition for several historic firsts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofwelch.com/home",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Comedian Steve Harvey was born in Welch in 1957, making the town the hometown of a nationally known entertainer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://wvexplorer.com/communities/cities-towns/welch-west-virginia/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Welch became McDowell County’s seat in 1892, before incorporation, after county records were secretly moved at night.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welch%2C_West_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A Norfolk Southern Railway station in Welch links the town to the former Norfolk and Western network, reflecting its railroad heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welch%2C_West_Virginia",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In 1960, Welch proclaimed itself “The Heart of the Nation’s Coal Bin,” underscoring its central role in West Virginia’s coal industry.",
